WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.160
Britt: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.990
we wanted to find all the differences

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.630
between McDonald's in
the US and Australia.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.493
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:10.920
Before we get started,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.170
I wanted to introduce our new host, Britt.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.290
She is going to be our "Food
Wars" expert down in Australia,

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.330
and I hope you guys love
her as much as I do.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.533
She is lovely.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.970
In the US, our fries come in four sizes,

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.730
kids, small, medium, and large.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.600
In Australia, our fries come
in three different sizes,

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.480
small, medium, and large.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.330
Nico: Let's weigh our largest fry.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.420
I am so impressed by
this stack, by the way.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.924
This is a masterpiece.

00:00:40.924 --> 00:00:43.200
Wow.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.670
Get a load of that stack of fries.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.110
Very impressive.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.127
That's it for me, bye!

00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:50.100
What about the iconic Big Mac?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.543
Let's weigh it.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.940
Some of our burger options

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.010
come in different sizes to the US.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.260
We have a single cheeseburger,

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.040
a double cheeseburger,
and a triple cheeseburger.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.050
Over here, the standard
McDonald's cheeseburger

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.530
only comes in two sizes,
the single or the double.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.780
Our McDonald's drinks come in four sizes,

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.935
extra small, which we could not get,

00:01:11.935 --> 00:01:14.070
small, medium, and large.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.890
Our drinks in Australia
come in three sizes,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.860
small, medium, and large.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.980
12 fluid ounces is the
size of a can of Coke,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.440
so it's so wild to me that that is

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.100
the smallest size of beverage
you can get at McDonald's.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.200
Let's measure our largest drink.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.540
Our largest drink came
out to 800 milliliters

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.990
when we're supposed to be getting 946.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.580
That is egregious!

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.234
That's so, so unfair!

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.284
Producer: It's not even 600!

00:01:42.284 --> 00:01:45.360
It's not even 600, but what number is it?

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.830
So, our large is coming
at 520 milliliters.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.820
650 to 520 is a massive difference.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.020
Daylight robbery.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.450
Chicken nuggets in the
US come in five sizes,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.000
a four-piece, a six-piece, a 10-piece,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.820
a 20-piece, and a 40-piece.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.790
Our chicken nuggets come in five sizes.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:10.650
We have a three-piece,
a six-piece, a 10-piece,

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:14.520
a 20-piece, and a 40-piece.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.090
Finally, another country
matches us with the 40-piece!

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:21.453
It's only taken us two years
of "Food Wars" to find one.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.860
Here is everything at
an Australian McDonald's

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.600
you won't find in the US.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.700
Here's everything at a US McDonald's

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.440
you won't find in Australia.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.000
There are a lot of things over here

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.720
that you can't find in the
States, like these socks.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.030
We're going to break
them down into categories

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.350
and go through them all.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.760
I really need to try these socks on

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.320
because they are amazing.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.660
Look at that. Fashion, fun.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:49.140
I'm going to feel like a
criminal with these bad boys.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.193
Hamburglar.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:54.630
Starting with the beef burgers,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:59.070
we have a classic Angus;
a barbecue bacon Angus;

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.770
a spicy, sticky barbecue Angus;

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.250
we have a triple cheeseburger;
big brekkie burger,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.520
which I just couldn't resist

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.470
and I really needed to try that.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.660
And then we have a McFeast,

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:14.160
and then we finish off
with the double Big Mac.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.053
It's massive.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:20.460
I think you taste more
meat than the actual sauce

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.170
with the combination of the meat.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.660
I think just a regular
Big Mac is probably better

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.980
because you get more flavor.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.170
So, if you look at these
burgers that we have here,

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:32.310
this Angus looks a little bit
more premium than the others.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.303
I definitely think there's
a culture in Australia

00:03:35.303 --> 00:03:39.600
that really enjoys high-quality
beef, high-quality burgers,

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.000
which is why these do so well here.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.340
Here are the exclusive burger options.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.190
We have a McDouble, my favorite,

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.530
and then we have two Quarter
Pounders with cheese.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.330
One just has bacon on it.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.210
I think what makes it different
than a double cheeseburger

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.440
is that the double cheeseburger

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.280
has two slices of cheese and no ketchup.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.740
Confirm or deny that right here for me.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.380
The McDouble also has thinner patties,

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.810
which I prefer to the thicker ones.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:10.290
Moving on, I do want to try
one of the Quarter Pounders.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.105
I'm going for the one with
bacon in it, because obviously.

00:04:13.105 --> 00:04:15.330
This looks like a perfect little burger.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.730
You could be in commercials!

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:18.900
Mm, that's good!

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:22.920
So, this is the Quarter
Pounder deluxe with cheese.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:26.700
Next, let's take a look at
our chicken and fish options

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.960
we have over here.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.070
First and starting strong,
we have a deluxe chicken.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.978
It's a grilled chicken

00:04:34.978 --> 00:04:38.460
with lettuce, tomato, mayo.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.600
It's aioli.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.780
And moving on, we have our McSpicy.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.253
Smells peppery.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.770
It's got a bit of a kick,

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.665
but I wouldn't say that it's ...

00:04:48.665 --> 00:04:51.900
oh, oh, it's the afterkick. It gets spicy.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.970
Oh, my gosh, it's creeping up on me.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.230
I actually really like this.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.480
Next one is the double McChicken.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.113
This is a heavy burger. Two
pieces of chicken on it.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.990
You're not missing out on this in America.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.370
Thumbs down, mm-mm.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:06.930
While we're talking about chicken,

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:10.800
we have a bunch of chicken
wraps here in Australia,

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.714
starting with the Caesar
grilled chicken McWrap,

00:05:13.714 --> 00:05:16.410
and we have a Caesar
crispy chicken McWrap.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.930
We have an aioli grilled chicken McWrap,

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.810
another aioli crispy chicken McWrap,

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:25.380
and then we have a grilled
chicken snack wrap.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.120
And we were supposed to have a wholemeal,

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.670
but there was no
wholemeal wraps available.

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.661
Let's try

00:05:31.661 --> 00:05:35.236
the aioli grilled chicken McWrap.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.230
That's really good.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.610
It's really light.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.510
Approved.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.740
I wouldn't mind having a look

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.950
at the crispy chicken Caesar wrap.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.590
The chicken inside as
well look really good.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.023
It's staring me down.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.740
It's better than the other
one, the aioli chicken.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.240
Burst of flavor in your mouth.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.560
Moving on to our chicken options,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.740
we have the spicy McCrispy,
the spicy McCrispy deluxe,

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.200
and the regular McCrispy deluxe.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.440
I think that "deluxe" in
McDonald's terminology

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.720
just means it has
lettuce and tomato on it.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.573
So, this is the spicy McCrispy.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:14.370
That is really good, and
it's actually so spicy.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.785
And finally, we have the
following salad options:

00:06:17.785 --> 00:06:20.730
classic chicken salad,

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.700
and then we also have a Caesar salad,

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:28.590
and we have a garden salad
that looks really sad.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.120
It's quite tragic, actually.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.942
Little seasoning for the Caesar salad.

00:06:32.942 --> 00:06:35.100
I don't really care about a salad.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.960
McDonald's US used to serve salads,

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.970
but they started disappearing from menus

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:41.730
during the pandemic
and have not reemerged.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.620
I for one do not miss them.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.260
I'm not going to McDonald's for a salad.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:49.860
If I wanted a salad, I'd just
go to a salad place. You know?

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.165
Australians can, of course,

00:06:51.165 --> 00:06:53.580
enjoy McDonald's iconic Happy Meals,

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.880
including some things you
won't find in America.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:01.680
The grilled chicken snack
wrap, grape tomatoes,

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.320
a Pop Top, which is an
apple juice equivalent.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.670
Imagine if you were a kid

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.250
and you were like, "Mom,
take me to Macca's,"

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.430
and you drove past and she gave you this.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.630
I like the healthy option,

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.520
but you'd be absolutely devastated.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.620
That is punishment. That is awful.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.180
And a little toy.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.658
Spot It! Classic.

00:07:19.658 --> 00:07:21.450
Spot what exactly?

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.400
Is this like ... what is this?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.080
This is too complicated for me.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.414
How would this ... this is really boring.

00:07:27.414 --> 00:07:29.220
I would hate this if I was a kid.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.050
No. Give me a Tamagotchi or something.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.490
I don't know. What you give kids? Like ...

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.670
Kids in the US are limited to
just a hamburger or nuggets

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.010
plus fries and apple slices.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:39.510
One thing I thought was interesting

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:42.780
is that you can't get a soda
with the Happy Meal anymore.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:45.630
They only really give you
juice options or milk,

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.100
which is what I have here.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.620
Our Happy Meal theme is "Crash Bandicoot,"

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.020
which I haven't seen since I was a child.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.140
I think I had this game
on, like, Nintendo 64.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.250
It's very old,

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.110
but I think it's, like, a new mobile game

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.910
collaboration that they're doing.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.640
I do want to see what my toy is.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.130
Spyro's Memory Card Game.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.570
It's a memory card game.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.500
That's not that good.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.870
I feel like the toys
have really gone downhill

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:10.770
since I was a kid.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:14.137
We used to get stuff. Like, good stuff.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.403
Wait, is this a card game or no?

00:08:18.925 --> 00:08:19.758
What?

00:08:19.758 --> 00:08:21.270
Oh, my God, it's like a little ...

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.470
oh, it's a tin.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.300
The cards are in the tin.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.750
That's actually kind of cute.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.680
This is not going to
satisfy the iPad kids.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.660
They're going to put this in the garbage.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.790
So, here's our little card game.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:37.680
It is kind of cute that they made the box

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.510
a little "Crash Bandicoot" crate.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:40.343
That's fun.

00:08:40.343 --> 00:08:42.390
That's the Happy Meal in the US.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:44.940
Here are the exclusive sides from Macca's.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:48.000
We have some McDonaldland cookies

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.880
and a Petit Miam strawberry yogurt.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.690
We do also have the mozzarella
sticks with chili jam.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:58.320
However, they were out
of stock of that today.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:01.710
Oh, my gosh, this smell
reminds me of my childhood.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.810
Can I pour this? I'm going to pour this.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.020
You've got Ronald McDonald,
duck with glasses on.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.463
I'm sure that's someone.

00:09:10.206 --> 00:09:11.760
They're hard cookies.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:12.810
But generally in Australia

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.790
our cookies are generally quite hard.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.440
I don't know why, but they're delicious.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.990
We actually don't have any sides in the US

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.300
that you can't also find in Australia.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.250
The one thing I wish that we had

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.560
that Australia has is
those mozzarella sticks.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.320
I would devour some
mozzarella sticks right now.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:29.580
It's that time.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:30.658
It's sauce talk.

00:09:30.658 --> 00:09:32.280
Sauce talk.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.740
We actually don't have very
many sauces to talk about.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.200
I have ranch, plain mustard,

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.110
and we're missing a
regular packet of honey.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:43.500
I'm not really sure why they
have honey as a sauce option.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.910
Like, what do you use that for?

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:46.920
I guess you could use it on the biscuits.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:48.150
I know what ranch tastes like.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.860
I know what mustard tastes like.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.210
We don't have to talk about it anymore.

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.307
Sauce talk is over.

00:09:53.307 --> 00:09:55.230
Here are the Aussie exclusive sauces.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:57.270
We have a wasabi-flavored mayo,

00:09:57.270 --> 00:10:02.220
a truffle-flavored mayo, aioli
sauce, and sweet mustard.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.210
All right, let's try them.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.343
So, this is the aioli.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:07.673
Yum.

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:08.970
Quite garlicky as well.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.623
So, this is the sweet mustard.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:14.580
It's just not a bit of me.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.920
But yeah, aioli is a classic here.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:17.820
Anything with garlic,

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:20.910
anything with a really strong flavor

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.024
that makes people want
to stay far away from you

00:10:23.024 --> 00:10:26.100
when you speak and breathe, we're onto it.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.160
If you actually manage to
wake up in time for breakfast,

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.620
then you'll find a ton of
exclusive breakfast items

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:32.970
here in the US.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:36.540
McDonald's actually did do
an all-day breakfast menu,

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.220
which was revolutionary.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.536
Lives were changed.

00:10:39.536 --> 00:10:42.319
And then in March of 2020 they stopped,

00:10:42.319 --> 00:10:45.540
and we went back to breakfast until 11.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.900
11 doesn't sound like
that early of a time,

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.035
but for me, yeah, it is.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:55.050
And in the US, you can obviously
get your breakfast sandwich

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:59.310
on a variety of vessels, like the biscuit.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:01.050
We also have the McGriddle,

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.960
which is essentially two little pancakes

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.610
with a bunch of syrup holes.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:09.660
So the syrup is already
incorporated into the pancake bun.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.390
And whoever thought of this as a sandwich,

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:15.510
something special happened,
something shifted,

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.160
because this is one of the greatest things

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.590
I've ever seen and tasted.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.880
We don't have that here,

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.270
but I can't say I'm particularly jealous.

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.880
The idea of having syrupy pancakes

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:30.840
as a bun with meat is just a bit weird.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:34.080
However, I know that you
guys rave on about it,

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.060
so I'd be really, really
inclined to try it

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:39.240
because I'd want to know
how it would actually taste.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.810
There's also the McMuffin,
which is an English muffin.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:44.880
There's also a variety
of different proteins

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.620
that you can get in
your breakfast sandwich.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:50.730
Like, I'm seeing ham, bacon, sausage,

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:53.790
and now steak, which was a shock to me.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.928
I didn't hear anything about McDonald's

00:11:55.928 --> 00:11:59.310
adding steak to its breakfast
menu, but we got it.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:02.193
Let's start with this steak biscuit.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.230
In my brain, when I saw the
steak on the menu, I was like,

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:09.480
wow, they're doing little bits of steak.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.070
That's actually so impressive.

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:14.620
This is a burger patty in
a breakfast-sandwich form.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.200
It doesn't taste bad.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.550
This is my favorite McGriddle.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.500
It's the bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.880
All those little dark spots,

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.190
those are the syrup holes.

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:24.930
These are always going to hit for me.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.100
They're good.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.045
This is the McMuffin with
Canadian bacon, cheese, and egg.

00:12:30.045 --> 00:12:32.940
The egg on this one is a
little different than the rest.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.493
It's supposed to be a freshly cracked egg.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.790
I wasn't in the room when this was made,

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.170
so I can't speak on that.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:43.323
But it looks different than
the folded egg, obviously.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.710
That was a little tough.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:49.923
And lastly, we have the sausage burrito.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.560
That's pretty good, I'm not gonna lie.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:55.020
Moving on to the breakfast meals.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.512
These are bigger portions.

00:12:56.512 --> 00:12:58.230
There's more stuff involved,

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.330
it's not just a quick little sandwich.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:01.770
We have the Big Breakfast.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:03.630
There's the Big Breakfast with hotcakes,

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.470
which comes with all of that
stuff, plus some hotcakes.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.140
There's the hotcakes with a sausage patty.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.240
And all the hotcake meals come with

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.710
whipped butter and syrup.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:14.580
Duh.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:18.135
The hotcakes at McDonald's
are a little ...

00:13:18.135 --> 00:13:19.500
they taste kind of fake,

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.990
like they don't taste like real pancakes,

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.610
but I'm a big fan of them.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.170
I don't know, there's
something very nostalgic

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.790
about the hotcakes for me.

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:28.590
We also have the fruit and maple oatmeal,

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.480
which comes with fruit

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:31.920
and I am assuming maple

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.350
already incorporated into the oatmeal.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:35.913
Let's pour these in.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.510
OK, this actually smells really good.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:40.623
Am I just hungry?

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:42.900
It's a good oatmeal.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.250
I would order that again.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:45.510
It doesn't taste too sweet.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.040
And the parts that are sweet are fruit,

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.960
so I don't really feel bad eating it.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:49.950
We only have a couple of

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:52.650
exclusive breakfast
bites here in Australia.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:57.450
We have the mighty McMuffin
or the big brekkie burger.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.150
If you can see, two patties,

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:04.440
onion, and a hash brown, cheese, egg.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.940
I don't think my mouth is going
to open up wide enough to...

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.953
All right, I'm slightly intimidated.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.370
That is so good.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.073
Unreal. I recommend that.

00:14:16.073 --> 00:14:19.710
So, now we have the mighty McMuffin.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.750
It's not a regular McMuffin.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:22.893
It's better than that.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.770
It's not as flavorful as this.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:28.830
This is a subtle explosion,
not a full earthquake.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.463
This is ... I'm going to have another bite

00:14:30.463 --> 00:14:32.310
because I actually really like it.

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:35.940
So, here we have all of our
McCafé exclusive drinks.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.610
First up we have the iced
French vanilla latte,

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.053
which sounds very good.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.620
It's sweet. That is very sweet.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.750
They're giving Dunkin'
a run for their money.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:48.660
It doesn't taste bad because
it's a French vanilla coffee,

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.460
but that's way too sweet for me.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.800
We also have that latte hot.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:55.200
Next, there's the iced
French vanilla coffee,

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.702
which, I actually might like this more.

00:14:57.702 --> 00:14:59.910
Yeah, this one is way better to me.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:02.760
It actually tastes more
like coffee and not milk.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:04.740
Next we have a caramel cappuccino.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:07.080
This is a vanilla cappuccino,

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:10.410
and we have the iced caramel macchiato.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.183
Let's try the caramel cappuccino.

00:15:14.057 --> 00:15:18.120
I'm not a huge fan of
the taste of this one.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:21.570
We're missing the
Americano and the frappé,

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:24.780
which I've had before. It is very sweet.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:28.140
You'll find Macca's McCafé items

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.780
in both the US and Australia,

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.990
but the offerings are pretty different.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.700
So, these are our McCafé drinks.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.170
We have our long black,

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.170
which is basically an
Americano but better.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:43.920
And we have our English
breakfast tea, our Earl Grey tea.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:48.690
We have a green tea, a
peppermint tea, a piccolo latte,

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:50.340
and a little babyccino.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.260
I'm really jealous of
those cute little coffees

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.400
that you have in Australia.

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.740
I want that little tiny baby cup.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:59.100
We have our iced long black,
our deluxe crème brûlée,

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.077
which is iced and not here.

00:16:01.077 --> 00:16:05.610
And we also have our iced
chocolate, a coffee frappé,

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:08.550
a deluxe caramel iced coffee.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:12.414
We have also a deluxe
hazelnut iced coffee.

00:16:12.414 --> 00:16:14.105
And then last but not least,

00:16:14.105 --> 00:16:17.530
our vanilla deluxe iced coffee.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:19.623
I really want to try this iced chocolate.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:21.780
That's not going to be
good for my stomach,

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.190
but this is really good.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:25.500
It's like a cocoa powder chocolate flavor.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:26.940
Like, it's not too rich.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:28.710
Teas at Macca's.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.780
I don't know anyone that would get a tea.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.820
I mean, unless you're,
like, a British expat.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.560
I want to try peppermint tea because ...

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.410
Did they put milk in
my peppermint tea too?

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:38.370
What?

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:41.403
Why would you put milk in a herbal tea?

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:45.450
Oh, that's putrid.

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:49.830
Did you know that McCafé was
actually created in Australia

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.470
in Melbourne in 1993?

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.000
The first café was opened

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.280
in Swanston Street, I'm pretty sure.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.230
We pride ourselves on our coffee,

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:00.000
especially people in Melbourne.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.730
Without Melbourne or Australia,

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.320
you wouldn't be having McCafé.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:06.060
So, thank you.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.443
I will take all the glory.

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.410
This is our McCafé food.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:12.330
We have a barbecue,
bacon, and cheese toastie,

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.400
which we don't have here.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:16.317
We have a ham and cheese toastie.

00:17:16.317 --> 00:17:18.810
We have a cheese and tomato toastie.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:20.790
We have a cheesy toastie.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.890
Banana bread with blueberries.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.690
We really like banana bread here.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.910
And then just your plain banana bread.

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.070
We usually stock raisin toast with butter,

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:31.110
but they were out of stock for that today.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.750
We have our double-chocolate muffin

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.880
and apple crumble muffin.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.400
We also have a chocolate doughnut.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.910
And because we like to
keep it a little bit fancy,

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.590
we have a chocolate macaron

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:47.130
and we also have a salted caramel macaron.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:49.770
Australians, we really love our caramel.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.050
Salted caramel, normal caramel.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.553
We have it with everything.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.640
That's a really nice salted caramel.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.140
Good job, Macca's.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.750
Another thing we're missing
here in the US McCafé

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.190
is the food.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:04.830
Those are all gone from the
menu, and we have a theory.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.120
We have a theory that it's because

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.270
they're opening up their
new CosMc's restaurant,

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:12.210
which is I guess a McCafé
turned into a restaurant.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:14.226
It's going to be, like, bakery items

00:18:14.226 --> 00:18:16.651
and coffees and just that.

00:18:16.651 --> 00:18:19.170
If you want to end your Macca's
meal with a sweet treat,

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:23.160
we have some exclusive
dessert options for you,

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.282
starting off with a Milo McFlurry.

00:18:25.282 --> 00:18:27.000
There was supposed to be a Malteser,

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.200
but they were all out of them.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:32.040
So we got the better
option, which is Milo.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.120
If you don't know what Milo is,

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:35.850
Milo is an Australian classic.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.440
You can put it in your drinks,

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.140
you can put it on ice cream.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.570
It's just a chocolate
powder that is so good.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:45.660
We didn't have a
raspberry and custard pie.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.220
They were sold out of that as well.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:51.420
We have a strawberry
sundae, a caramel sundae,

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.653
and then we have

00:18:54.653 --> 00:18:58.320
a Cadbury Flake soft serve.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:03.060
Oh, my gosh, the Flake has
been consumed by the ice cream.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:05.101
You can't even see the Flake anymore.

00:19:05.101 --> 00:19:06.870
RIP.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:11.340
We have our frozen Fanta
raspberry, frozen Fanta blueberry,

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:16.110
frozen Fanta mango, and
our frozen Fanta grape.

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.300
I really want to try this Milo McFlurry.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.450
Literally what my dreams
have been made of.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:25.680
This is unreal.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.420
This is so yum.

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.370
Our only exclusive dessert option

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.110
is the chocolate chip cookies,

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:34.020
which I think in the realm
of fast-food cookies,

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:35.910
this is definitely at the top

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:38.970
because they stay soft and
they're actually pretty good.

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:41.640
A perfectly fine chocolate chip cookie.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.470
Outside of McCafé drinks,

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:46.590
we have a couple of exclusive
soft drinks here in Australia.

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:49.710
We have a vanilla Coke,
we have a Coke zero,

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.720
and sparkling water.

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:54.030
While it's technically not an exclusive,

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:56.850
it's also worth noting that in Australia,

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.580
we call our milkshakes thickshakes.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.850
The reason why we call
our milkshakes thickshakes

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:05.280
is because a milkshake is
different in Australia.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.190
So, milkshake is literally
just a sweetened milk.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.200
So if you were to get
a strawberry milkshake,

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:14.070
it would just be a really
thin strawberry-tasting milk.

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:17.310
With a thickshake, it's
a thicker consistency.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:19.590
In front of me though,
I have the sweet tea,

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:21.210
the orange Hi-C,

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.220
and the two milk options that they offer,

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.070
which is regular and a chocolate milk.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:29.880
Do not be fooled by this very
naturally occurring color.

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.280
It is not real fruit juice.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.583
Hi-C is something entirely its own thing.

00:20:37.479 --> 00:20:39.390
Australians love McDonald's,

00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:42.450
or it's more commonly
known here as Macca's.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.830
The nickname is so popular

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:46.200
that McDonald's has
actually leaned into it

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.580
and formally embraced it.

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:48.810
It's always called Macca's.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.270
That being said, though,
it can get confusing,

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:55.020
as Macca can also refer
to anyone with a surname

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.980
that starts with M-C or Mac, M-A-C.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:02.338
So McDonald's equals Macca's,

00:21:02.338 --> 00:21:07.290
but Paul McCartney, for an
example, is also called Macca.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.390
So the context is really crucial here.

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:12.630
McDonald's has the
second-highest number of stores

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:14.730
of any fast-food chain in Australia,

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.470
ranking just below Subway.

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:18.660
That number stands to rise too,

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:22.530
with reports saying that
McDonald's is planning to spend

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:24.540
a billion Australian dollars

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.420
opening and renovating
stores in the coming years.

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:32.220
Anecdotally, I think Macca's
is way more popular than Subway

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:33.420
just because it's convenient

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.390
and I think everyone
always craves a burger,

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.730
and I feel like the idea of Subway

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.740
isn't as appealing as McDonald's is.

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:43.830
There are over 13,000
locations here in the US,

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.240
so I think it's fair to say

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.790
that Americans love their McDonald's.

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:51.210
You can't go, like, a few miles

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.250
without seeing golden arches.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.050
They are absolutely everywhere.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:58.440
I don't know a single
person who's never tried it.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:01.440
I don't think America has a national dish,

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:04.140
but if we did, I feel like it would be

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:07.890
a burger, fries, a
milkshake, and/or a soda.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:11.070
Like, that's so American in my brain.

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:13.290
And that's why McDonald's in itself

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:15.840
feels like such an American food chain.

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:18.840
McDonald's Australia has
tried to adapt its menu

00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:20.910
to local tastes over the years.

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:22.620
One of the examples was that

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:26.370
of the recent potato scallop controversy.

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:28.320
Yes, I know it sounds bizarre.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:30.703
What is a potato scallop?
So many questions.

00:22:30.703 --> 00:22:33.690
But in January of 2023,

00:22:33.690 --> 00:22:36.060
Macca's announced a new menu item,

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:38.580
and it was called a potato
scallop with chicken salt.

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:40.890
So, this sparked an online debate,

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:43.770
as the states of Victoria and Tasmania

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:46.680
refer to this as a potato cake,

00:22:46.680 --> 00:22:49.980
whereas other areas call
it a potato fritter.

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:53.220
Some claim that the name is
an insult to potato cakes.

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.700
To be honest, I don't care.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:22:58.500
But so many Australians do,

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:01.140
and it is, like, institutionalized in them

00:23:01.140 --> 00:23:03.780
that they need to care
about what a potato cake

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:04.980
is actually called.

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:06.990
Basically, if you also don't
know what a potato cake is,

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.940
it's literally just a deep-fried potato

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:11.100
with chicken salt on top of it.

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:13.830
And chicken salt is also
an Australian classic.

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:15.900
It's sadly not on the menu anymore.

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:19.350
So at least that debate can
be put on hold, for now.

00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:21.360
In America, I would say that McDonald's

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:24.120
is pretty much exactly
the same everywhere.

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.350
I don't think that they adapt

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:27.390
to local tastes to that degree,

00:23:27.390 --> 00:23:30.240
but they do vary from country to country.

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:32.190
