00:26:40.590 --> 00:26:43.333
Here are the ingredients
of an Australian Big Mac.

00:26:43.333 --> 00:26:47.253
A key distinction between the
beef in Australia and the US

00:26:47.253 --> 00:26:51.311
is the majority of cattle
in our country is grass-fed,

00:26:51.311 --> 00:26:54.480
while in the US, beef is mostly grain-fed.

00:26:54.480 --> 00:26:56.580
Grain-fed tends to have a bit more

00:26:56.580 --> 00:26:59.100
of a uniform taste and texture,

00:26:59.100 --> 00:27:01.290
whereas grass-fed is heavily influenced

00:27:01.290 --> 00:27:03.750
by seasonal and regional factors,

00:27:03.750 --> 00:27:05.610
resulting in a diverse range

00:27:05.610 --> 00:27:08.220
of complex flavors and textures.

00:27:08.220 --> 00:27:10.405
Additionally, the high concentration

00:27:10.405 --> 00:27:13.110
of beta-carotene in grass

00:27:13.110 --> 00:27:15.390
contributes to a more pronounced taste

00:27:15.390 --> 00:27:17.790
in the fat found in grass-fed beef.

00:27:17.790 --> 00:27:19.740
The taste can be quite different,

00:27:19.740 --> 00:27:23.040
and Australians take pride in their meat.

00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:27.720
A US Big Mac contains all of this.

00:27:27.720 --> 00:27:28.890
A few things to note.

00:27:28.890 --> 00:27:30.810
The pickle slices contain alum,

00:27:30.810 --> 00:27:32.340
which is used to dissolve steel,

00:27:32.340 --> 00:27:36.150
and polysorbate 80, which has
been linked to colon cancer.

00:27:36.150 --> 00:27:38.313
This means we can cue the dancing mice.

